        <briefdescription>
<para>Writes a text to a file, without the ANSI colour sequences. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The text may contain ANSI colour sequences, added when the console is a terminal, which must not reach the file. They are removed while writing: each <computeroutput>ESC [</computeroutput>, followed by any digits and semicolons, and terminated by <computeroutput>m</computeroutput>, is skipped, and the text between the sequences is written unchanged. Any other use of <computeroutput>ESC</computeroutput> is written as is. No line ending is appended.</para>
